  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform magnetic field of 0.4 T acts perpendicular to a circular copper disc 20 cm in radius. The disc is having a uniform angular velocity of $10 \\pi \\mathrm{rad} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}$ about an axis through its centre and perpendicular to the disc. What is the potential difference developed between the axis of the disc and the rim ? $(\\pi=3.14)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
